    "updated_at": "2023-09-28T19:39:32Z",
    "body": "To clarify use case,  the reason for initializing in this fashion is due to the necessity of include multiplicity info.  An attempt to directly manifest a tq.Molecule object for atoms like lithium will fail due to spin;\r\n\r\n```python\r\ntmol=tq.Molecule(\"Li 0 0 0\",basis_set=basis,backend='pyscf') \r\n```\r\nwill fail with relevant traceback\r\n\r\n```\r\nRuntimeError: Electron number 3 and spin 0 are not consistent\r\nNote mol.spin = 2S = Nalpha - Nbeta, not 2S+1\r\n```\r\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
